<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
<title>cash: third-party licences</title>
<style>
  body { font-family: system-ui, sans-serif; max-width: 60em; margin: 2em auto; padding: 0 1em; line-height: 1.5; }
  pre { white-space: pre-wrap; background: #f4f4f4; padding: 1em; font-size: 0.85em; }
  ul.crates { columns: 3 14em; }
  @media (prefers-color-scheme: dark) {
    body { background: #1b1b1b; color: #ddd; }
    pre { background: #262626; }
    a { color: #8ab4f8; }
  }
</style>
</head>
<body>
<h1>Third-party licences</h1>
<p>cash.exe is built from the Rust crates below. Each licence text applies to the crates
listed above it. cash's own licence is in LICENSE, and the code it absorbed from brush and
lsd is described in NOTICE.</p>
<h2>Overview</h2>
<ul>
{{#each overview}}
  <li><a href="#{{id}}">{{name}}</a>: {{count}} crates</li>
{{/each}}
</ul>
{{#each licenses}}
<h2 id="{{id}}">{{name}}</h2>
<ul class="crates">
{{#each used_by}}
  <li><a href="{{#if crate.repository}}{{crate.repository}}{{else}}https://crates.io/crates/{{crate.name}}{{/if}}">{{crate.name}} {{crate.version}}</a></li>
{{/each}}
</ul>
<pre>{{text}}</pre>
{{/each}}
</body>
</html>
